{;; kmet's RFC 0014 provider lib (see README.md in this dir). EMPTY BY
 ;; DESIGN: every JDK gap this lib was created for is runtime surface now
 ;; (jolt-bugs.md records the closures), so it claims and installs nothing.
 ;; The scaffolding stays — the next gap adds its class below and its
 ;; member registration to src/jolt/kmet/providers.clj's install!.
 ;;
 ;; A class the runtime IMPLEMENTS cannot be claimed by anybody — a member
 ;; of it that is missing needs the guarded-require convention instead
 ;; (AGENTS.md's jolt/ section). RSA is not on this list either —
 ;; jolt.crypto provides it (EC and RSA), so the claims for
 ;; java.security.Signature / KeyPairGenerator / KeyFactory live in
 ;; crypto's own :jolt/provides (jolt allows a class only one provider).
 ;;
 ;; The native libs (libcrypto/libssl) and the crypto java.* classes come
 ;; from io.github.jolt-lang/crypto. This lib does NOT require it: crypto's
 ;; own :jolt/provides claims resolve its classes on the first reference,
 ;; whatever loaded first — RFC 0014 gives a class one provider, and a
 ;; declared provider owns the members it registers. jolt dedupes natives by
 ;; :name, so the app declaring crypto once is enough.
 ;;
 ;; Inert on bb/JVM: nothing in the bb classpath ever requires a jolt.kmet.*
 ;; namespace.
 :jolt/min-version "0.8.0"

 :paths ["src"]

 ;; SCI for the sci backend's suite on Jolt (RFC 0014 lib: this deps.edn is
 ;; jolt/JVM-only, so the pin lives here rather than in the root deps.edn,
 ;; which hosts may treat as a host-vendored namespace). Extension contexts
 ;; do not go through SCI on Jolt any more — they run on the runtime's own
 ;; loader — but the sci backend is still the bb/JVM one and `jolt test`
 ;; kmet.loader.test-sci-loader proves it there, which needs the dep.
 ;; babashka bundles SCI, so only jolt/JVM resolve it — 0.13.53 is the
 ;; jolt-gated version (jolt's own vendor/sci is 0.13.53; the latest
 ;; 0.15.x needs clojure.core/Inst, absent on jolt).
 :deps {org.babashka/sci {:mvn/version "0.13.53"}}

 ;; The classes this lib installs (RFC 0014): jolt autoloads the install
 ;; namespace on the FIRST reference to one of these, whatever the registry
 ;; state (a claim is authority over who implements a class, not a fallback
 ;; for an absent one). Empty while the lib is a no-op.
 :jolt/provides {}}
